.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/spec-v1-audit-log.schema.md:501:| `salt_rotation_registered` (v2.58) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `reason` (str — CLOSED enum {`first_mint`, `migration_mint`, `other`}; anything else COERCED to `other`, never echoed), `salt_scope` (str — fixed vocabulary of one: `project`, the ADR-079 S318 salt unit; anything else COERCED), `slug_sha256` (str — 16-hex sha256 PREFIX of the native project slug; shape-checked, malformed COERCED to the sentinel `"invalid"`, never echoed), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-182 W1 — the ONE sanctioned, REGISTERED salt-rotation event (ADR-079 S318 amendment §2: minting a per-project `.salt` is observable in the chain, never silent; the pre-S318 `get_instance_salt()` minted with no error, no log, no signal). Producer: `_lib/injection_salt.py::_register_mint` via LAZY `emit_generic` at mint time only (no module-load coupling; a `salt-minted.json` sidecar next to the salt is the forensic ground truth when the emit path is unavailable). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_SALT_ROTATION_REGISTERED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the slug/path TEXT, the salt bytes, the salt path. NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
