    24	## No rotation — with exactly ONE sanctioned, REGISTERED exception
    25	
    26	Salt is generated once per PROJECT (ADR-079 S318 amendment: the salt
    27	unit is the project, resolved via ``_lib/runtime_paths`` — the
    28	per-``$HOME`` reading made ``prompt_sha256`` correlate ACROSS projects,
    29	the exact oracle this module exists to close) and never rotated.
    30	Rotating the salt would invalidate ``prompt_sha256`` correlations
    31	across all historical audit events (the chief use of the field).
    32	
    33	The one exception is the PLAN-182 migration itself: the project that
    34	inherits the historical chain (W2 custody decision) inherits the
    35	legacy ``.salt`` byte-for-byte; every OTHER project mints fresh — and
    36	that minting is OBSERVABLE, never silent (the pre-S318 code minted
    37	with no error, no log, no signal — silent rotation against this very
    38	section). Every mint now (a) writes a ``salt-minted.json`` marker
    39	sidecar next to the salt (forensic ground truth) and (b) best-effort
    40	emits the registered ``salt_rotation_registered`` chain event.
    41	
    42	## Thread safety
    43	
    44	The module-level ``_CACHED_SALT`` is read-once-write-once, and the
    45	FIRST MINT is elected by the filesystem: ``_generate_and_persist``
    46	creates with ``O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW``, so exactly one process
    47	wins and every loser RE-READS the winner's bytes.
    48	
    49	rc.1 re-pass part 6 C2 — this section used to accept the race, on the
